But we still need to fight him.

268
00:16:32,010 --> 00:16:33,230
That's all I know.

269
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:36,640
You and I won't find much joy while we're here.

270
00:16:37,630 --> 00:16:39,370
But we can keep up the life.

271
00:16:39,990 --> 00:16:42,630
We can defend those who can't defend themselves.

272
00:16:45,850 --> 00:16:48,720
I am the shield that guards the realm of men.

273
00:16:48,960 --> 00:16:51,450
Maybe we don't need to understand anymore than that.

274
00:16:52,630 --> 00:16:53,940
Maybe that's enough.

275
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:55,600
Aye.

276
00:16:57,730 --> 00:16:58,890
Maybe that's enough.

277
00:17:07,970 --> 00:17:09,710
That's what I saw in the fire.

278
00:17:11,040 --> 00:17:12,820
A mountain like an arrow head.

279
00:17:15,190 --> 00:17:15,990
Are you sure?

280
00:17:19,390 --> 00:17:20,710
We're getting close.

281
00:17:29,330 --> 00:17:30,720
Do you know what I like about you?

282
00:17:33,090 --> 00:17:35,500
- I honestly don't. - You're not a hero.

283
00:17:36,230 --> 00:17:37,000
Oh.

284
00:17:38,430 --> 00:17:40,530
I've been heroic on occasion.

285
00:17:40,800 --> 00:17:43,350
I once charged through the Mud Gate of King's Landing.

286
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:45,190
I don't want you to be a hero.

287
00:17:45,400 --> 00:17:47,990
Heroes do stupid things and they die.

288
00:17:48,670 --> 00:17:51,470
Drogo, Jorah, Daario, even this...

289
00:17:52,880 --> 00:17:54,090
Jon Snow--

290
00:17:54,670 --> 00:17:56,440
they all try to outdo each other.

291
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:59,210
Who can do the stupidest, bravest thing...

292
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:01,630
It's interesting, these heroes you name...

293
00:18:01,630 --> 00:18:03,170
Drogo, Jorah,

294
00:18:03,170 --> 00:18:04,880
Daarios, even this...

295
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:06,790
Jon Snow.

296
00:18:07,390 --> 00:18:08,910
They all fell in love with you.

297
00:18:09,230 --> 00:18:10,480
Jon Snow is not in love with me.

298
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,790
Oh, my mistake.

299
00:18:11,990 --> 00:18:13,760
I suppose he stares at you longingly

300
00:18:13,760 --> 00:18:16,580
because he's hopeful for a successful military alliance.

301
00:18:20,210 --> 00:18:21,530
He's too little for me.

302
00:18:23,220 --> 00:18:24,470
I didn't mean...

303
00:18:24,470 --> 00:18:26,770
As heroes go he is quite little.

304
00:18:27,390 --> 00:18:28,750
I know you're brave.

305
00:18:30,170 --> 00:18:32,350
I wouldn't have chosen a coward as my Hand.

306
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:37,860
So...

307
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:41,950
if all goes well, I'll finally get to meet your sister.

308
00:18:43,930 --> 00:18:45,520
From everything you've told me about her

309
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:48,090
she's rather murder me than speak.

310
00:18:49,350 --> 00:18:50,610
First she'd torture you

311
00:18:50,610 --> 00:18:52,860
in some horrible way, then she'd murder you.

312
00:18:54,190 --> 00:18:57,050
Nobody trusts my sister less than I do, believe me.

313
00:18:57,780 --> 00:18:59,360
But if we go to the capital,

314
00:18:59,530 --> 00:19:02,450
we'll go with two armies, we'll go with three dragons.

315
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:03,760
And anyone touches you,

316
00:19:03,760 --> 00:19:06,070
King's Landing burns down to the foundation stone.

317
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,270
And right now she's thinking of how to set a trap.

318
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:09,300
Of course she is.

319
00:19:09,550 --> 00:19:11,940
And she's wondering what trap you're laying for her.

320
00:19:11,990 --> 00:19:12,840
Are we?

321
00:19:14,250 --> 00:19:15,710
Laying any traps?

322
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:20,850
If we want to create a new and better world,

323
00:19:21,110 --> 00:19:24,190
I'm not sure deceit and mass murder are the best ways to start.

324
00:19:24,190 --> 00:19:26,700
Which war was won without deceit and mass murder?

325
00:19:28,610 --> 00:19:30,720
Yes, you'll need to be ruthless

326
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:32,330
if you're going to win the throne.

327
00:19:32,620 --> 00:19:34,540
You need to inspire a degree of fear.

328
00:19:34,540 --> 00:19:36,880
But fear is all Cersei has.

329
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,480
It's all my father had, and Joffrey.

330
00:19:39,980 --> 00:19:41,820
It makes their power brittle.

331
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:44,720
Because everyone beneath them longs to see them dead.

332
00:19:45,670 --> 00:19:48,170
Aegon Targaryen got quite a long way on fear.

333
00:19:48,170 --> 00:19:49,080
He did.

334
00:19:49,850 --> 00:19:52,210
But you once spoke to me about breaking the wheel.

335
00:19:52,350 --> 00:19:53,970
Aegon built the wheel.

336
00:19:54,740 --> 00:19:56,210
If that's the kind of queen you want to be,

337
00:19:56,210 --> 00:19:57,060
how are you different from

338
00:19:57,060 --> 00:19:58,960
all the other tyrants that came before you?

339
00:19:58,990 --> 00:20:01,100
So we walk into the lion's den?

340
00:20:02,290 --> 00:20:05,160
My brother promised me he'd keep a grip on the Lannister forces.

341
00:20:05,160 --> 00:20:08,500
Forgive me, but I don't care about any Lannister promises.

342
00:20:09,480 --> 00:20:10,630
Except yours.

343
00:20:10,920 --> 00:20:12,530
And I promised him

344
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:15,720
I'd keep you from doing anything impulsive.

345
00:20:16,580 --> 00:20:17,870
Impulsive?

346
00:20:21,510 --> 00:20:23,710
This will be a difficult negotiation.

347
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:27,460
We're sitting down with people who want to see us both headless.

348
00:20:27,870 --> 00:20:30,340
My sister is likely to say something provocative.

349
00:20:30,340 --> 00:20:31,140
And?

350
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:34,860
And you've been known to lose your temper from time to time.

351
00:20:34,950 --> 00:20:38,170
- As all our great leaders do... - When have I lost my temper?

352
00:20:39,870 --> 00:20:41,090
Burning the Tarlys for instance.

353
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,920
That was not impulsive.

354
00:20:42,920 --> 00:20:45,150
That was necessary.

355
00:20:45,550 --> 00:20:47,300
- Perhaps. - Perhaps.

356
00:20:48,410 --> 00:20:51,050
Perhaps the father needed to die and not the son.

357
00:20:51,260 --> 00:20:52,590
Perhaps they both needed time to

358
00:20:52,590 --> 00:20:55,640
contemplate the mistakes in the solitude of a cold cell.

359
00:20:56,320 --> 00:20:58,540
We had no time to discuss the possibility

360
00:20:58,540 --> 00:21:00,580
before you ended their possibilities.

361
00:21:00,580 --> 00:21:01,760
One can be forgiven for thinking

362
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:03,680
you're taking your family's side in this debate.

363
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,710
I am taking their side.

364
00:21:05,910 --> 00:21:07,800
You need to take your enemy's side.

365
00:21:07,800 --> 00:21:09,680
You need to see things the way they do.

366
00:21:09,690 --> 00:21:11,760
And you need to see things the way they do

367
00:21:11,760 --> 00:21:13,650
if you're gonna anticipate their actions,

368
00:21:13,650 --> 00:21:16,140
respond effectively and beat them.

369
00:21:16,970 --> 00:21:19,140
Which I want you to do very much.

370
00:21:19,390 --> 00:21:20,720
Because I believe in you

371
00:21:20,920 --> 00:21:22,680
and the world you want to build.

372
00:21:23,920 --> 00:21:25,450
But the world you want to build

373
00:21:25,720 --> 00:21:29,190
doesn't get build all at once. Probably not in a single lifetime.

374
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:32,690
How do we ensure your vision endures?

375
00:21:33,380 --> 00:21:36,350
After you break the wheel, how do we make sure it stays broken?

376
00:21:38,710 --> 00:21:43,060
You want to know who sits on the Iron Throne after I'm dead, is that it?

377
00:21:44,700 --> 00:21:46,450
You say you can't have children.

378
00:21:47,120 --> 00:21:49,650
But there are other ways of choosing a successor.

379
00:21:50,030 --> 00:21:52,000
The Night's Watch has one method.

380
00:21:52,160 --> 00:21:53,330
The Ironborn folk,

381
00:21:53,330 --> 00:21:54,550
among their many flaws have another...

382
00:21:54,550 --> 00:21:57,070
We will discuss the succession after I wear the crown.

383
00:21:57,070 --> 00:21:58,910
Your Grace, I saw hundreds of arrows

384
00:21:58,910 --> 00:22:01,100
fly towards you when you fought on Blackwater Rush,

385
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:03,350
and I saw hundred of arrows miss.

386
00:22:03,450 --> 00:22:05,730
But any one of them could have found your heart and end...

387
00:22:05,730 --> 00:22:08,170
You've been thinking about my death quite a bit, haven't you?

388
00:22:09,250 --> 00:22:10,750
Is this one of the items you've discussed

389
00:22:10,750 --> 00:22:12,100
with your brother in King's Landing?

390
00:22:12,100 --> 00:22:14,400
I'm trying to serve you by planning on the long term.

391
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:16,340
Perhaps if you'd planned for the short term,

392
00:22:16,340 --> 00:22:18,390
we wouldn't have lost Dorne and Highgarden.

393
00:22:21,670 --> 00:22:23,600
We will discuss the succession

394
00:22:23,960 --> 00:22:25,780
after I wear the crown.

395
00:23:04,290 --> 00:23:05,260
Look.

396
00:23:14,410 --> 00:23:15,490
A bear.

397
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,280
Big fucker.

398
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:28,060
The bears have blue eyes.

399
00:25:33,470 --> 00:25:35,440
We have to get him back to Eastwatch.

400
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:38,330
Flask.

401
00:25:57,770 --> 00:25:58,640
Go on.

402
00:26:15,710 --> 00:26:16,690
You all right?

403
00:26:17,150 --> 00:26:19,600
I just got bit by a dead bear.

404
00:26:20,620 --> 00:26:21,550
Aye.

405
00:26:22,150 --> 00:26:23,130
You did.

406
00:26:25,540 --> 00:26:26,910
Funny old life.

407
00:26:29,090 --> 00:26:29,990
Alright then.

408
00:26:31,090 --> 00:26:32,050
We're off.

409
00:26:58,820 --> 00:27:00,990
- Where did she get it? - I don't know.

410
00:27:02,020 --> 00:27:03,720
She seems very resourceful.

411
00:27:06,890 --> 00:27:07,880
You're worried.

412
00:27:08,380 --> 00:27:10,650
We're asking 20,000 men to fight with us

413
00:27:10,650 --> 00:27:13,290
in the worst winter any of them have ever seen.

414
00:27:13,820 --> 00:27:16,460
The weather will be the least of their problem.

415
00:27:16,790 --> 00:27:19,550
Many of them will be happy to find a good reason to go home.

416
00:27:19,550 --> 00:27:20,710
You question their loyalty?

417
00:27:20,720 --> 00:27:22,700
Their loyalty is to Jon.

418
00:27:22,980 --> 00:27:25,500
Jon is not here. I haven't heard from him in weeks.

419
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:27,270
You're the Lady of Winterfell.

420
00:27:27,570 --> 00:27:30,570
The King chose you to rule in his absence.

421
00:27:32,090 --> 00:27:33,520
And rule you have.

422
00:27:34,030 --> 00:27:35,190
Wisely.

423
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:36,740
Ably.

424
00:27:37,470 --> 00:27:39,280
They say that, they respect you.

425
00:27:39,830 --> 00:27:41,460
Some may even prefer you.

426
00:27:41,520 --> 00:27:42,740
Yes, they turned their backs on Jon

427
00:27:42,740 --> 00:27:44,430
when it was time to retake Winterfell

428
00:27:44,430 --> 00:27:45,600
and then they named him their king

429
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:47,570
and now they're ready to turn their backs on him again.

430
00:27:47,810 --> 00:27:50,070
How far would you trust men like that?

431
00:27:50,180 --> 00:27:52,230
They're all bloody wind vanes.

432
00:27:52,230 --> 00:27:54,600
If they found out I wrote that letter...

433
00:27:54,630 --> 00:27:55,250
a woman who's already

434
00:27:55,250 --> 00:27:58,260
married not one but two enemies of her House...

435
00:27:59,450 --> 00:28:02,420
By the time Jon comes back, he'll have no army left.

436
00:28:02,420 --> 00:28:03,690
Arya is not like them.

437
00:28:06,640 --> 00:28:07,870
She's your sister.

438
00:28:08,760 --> 00:28:09,760
You may have disagreements,

439
00:28:09,770 --> 00:28:11,600
but she would never betray her family.

440
00:28:12,330 --> 00:28:14,920
She would if she thought I was going to betray Jon.

441
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:16,800
Is that what she thinks?

442
00:28:16,810 --> 00:28:18,460
I don't know what she thinks.

443
00:28:18,790 --> 00:28:20,350
I don't know her anymore.

444
00:28:23,190 --> 00:28:24,700
Perhaps Lady Brienne can help.

445
00:28:28,050 --> 00:28:31,440
She's sworn to protect both of Catelyn Stark girls.

446
00:28:31,910 --> 00:28:32,910
Is she not?

447
00:28:34,800 --> 00:28:35,700
She is.

448
00:28:40,790 --> 00:28:44,330
And if one of you were planning to harm the other in any way,

449
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,630
wouldn't she be honor bound to intercede?

450
00:28:49,810 --> 00:28:50,640
She would.

451
00:29:04,320 --> 00:29:06,160
Something I've always wanted to know.

452
00:29:06,610 --> 00:29:07,480
Alright.

453
00:29:07,810 --> 00:29:11,250
How drunk were you when you charged through the breach on Pyke?

454
00:29:12,340 --> 00:29:15,560
For being honest, I don't remember charging through the breach.

455
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:20,040
Some of the lads told me about it the next morning.

456
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:23,300
Some damn good scrap.

457
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:24,490
Alright.

458
00:29:25,980 --> 00:29:27,840
It was a proper scrap.

459
00:29:28,310 --> 00:29:30,880
The Ironborn thought you were some kind of god

460
00:29:31,660 --> 00:29:34,060
when you were waving that flaming sword.

461
00:29:35,480 --> 00:29:37,990
I thought you were the bravest man I ever saw.

462
00:29:39,090 --> 00:29:40,570
Just the drunkest.

463
00:30:21,730 --> 00:30:22,950
Where's the rest of them?

464
00:30:23,170 --> 00:30:25,180
If we wait long enough we will find out.

465
00:32:55,900 --> 00:32:57,040
Run back to Eastwatch.

466
00:32:57,040 --> 00:32:59,360
Get a raven to Daenerys, tell her what's happened.

467
00:32:59,360 --> 00:33:01,250
- I'm not leaving you. - You're the fastest.

468
00:33:01,250 --> 00:33:02,370
Go! Now!

469
00:33:04,080 --> 00:33:06,250
You're faster without the hammer. Give it!

470
00:33:06,620 --> 00:33:07,580
Give it!

471
00:33:15,770 --> 00:33:17,880
- Run! - Run!

472
00:33:18,360 --> 00:33:19,410
Come on!

473
00:33:26,290 --> 00:33:27,490
Stop!

474
00:33:45,610 --> 00:33:46,520
Go!

475
00:36:34,550 --> 00:36:35,520
What happened?

476
00:36:36,700 --> 00:36:37,860
Where are the others?

477
00:36:38,160 --> 00:36:39,120
Raven.

478
00:36:39,710 --> 00:36:41,120
We need to send the raven.

479
00:36:41,260 --> 00:36:43,280
Get the maester! Now!

480
00:37:24,590 --> 00:37:25,550
Thoros?

481
00:37:29,620 --> 00:37:30,560
Thoros!

482
00:37:48,970 --> 00:37:51,540
They say it's one of the better ways to go.

483
00:38:05,210 --> 00:38:06,220
Lord of Light,

484
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:08,990
show us the way.

485
00:38:09,850 --> 00:38:11,070
Come to us in our darkness

486
00:38:11,070 --> 00:38:13,080
and lead your servant into the light.

487
00:38:18,760 --> 00:38:20,270
We have to burn this body.

488
00:38:23,950 --> 00:38:25,720
We'll all be close behind him

489
00:38:26,380 --> 00:38:30,030
unless the Lord of Light is kind enough to send us a bit of fire.

490
00:38:39,040 --> 00:38:40,070
Lord of Light.

491
00:38:41,500 --> 00:38:43,200
Come to us in our darkness.

492
00:38:44,320 --> 00:38:46,650
For the night is dark and full of terrors.

493
00:39:10,860 --> 00:39:12,400
We'll all freeze soon.

494
00:39:13,900 --> 00:39:15,330
And so will the water.

495
00:39:19,700 --> 00:39:21,610
When you killed the white walker,

496
00:39:22,560 --> 00:39:25,220
almost all the dead that followed fell.

497
00:39:26,410 --> 00:39:27,340
Why?

498
00:39:28,300 --> 00:39:30,290
Maybe he was the one who turned them.

499
00:39:31,650 --> 00:39:33,260
We can go for the walkers.

500
00:39:34,130 --> 00:39:36,570
- Maybe we'll stand a chance. - No.

501
00:39:38,200 --> 00:39:40,420
We need to take that thing back with us.

502
00:39:44,290 --> 00:39:46,670
There's a raven flying for Dragonstone now.

503
00:39:47,040 --> 00:39:49,350
Daenerys is our only chance.

504
00:39:49,920 --> 00:39:50,790
No.

505
00:39:51,970 --> 00:39:53,060
There's another.

506
00:39:55,650 --> 00:39:56,840
Kill him.

507
00:39:58,090 --> 00:39:59,560
He turned them all.

508
00:40:04,340 --> 00:40:05,550
You don't understand...

509
00:40:07,310 --> 00:40:08,770
The Lord brought you back...

510
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:10,270
he brought me back...

511
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:12,840
No one else. Just us.

512
00:40:14,130 --> 00:40:16,190
Did he do it to watch us freeze to death?

513
00:40:18,560 --> 00:40:21,630
Careful, Beric. You lost your priest.

514
00:40:22,210 --> 00:40:23,920
This is your last life.

515
00:40:23,920 --> 00:40:26,020
I've been waiting for the end for a long time.

516
00:40:27,230 --> 00:40:29,350
Maybe the Lord brought me here to find it.

517
00:40:30,380 --> 00:40:32,570
Every Lord I've ever met's been a cunt.

518
00:40:33,620 --> 00:40:36,080
Don't see why the Lord of Light should be any different.

519
00:40:49,630 --> 00:40:50,580
My lady.

520
00:41:01,110 --> 00:41:02,040
My lady?

521
00:41:03,270 --> 00:41:04,910
It's an invitation

522
00:41:05,300 --> 00:41:07,020
to King's Landing.

523
00:41:13,510 --> 00:41:16,490
- My lady, you are the Lady of Winterfell. - I am.

524
00:41:16,640 --> 00:41:20,040
And you will represent my interests at this gathering as you see them.

525
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:23,370
They invited you. They want you there.

526
00:41:24,680 --> 00:41:26,830
I will not set foot in King's Landing while

527
00:41:26,830 --> 00:41:28,980
Cersei Lannister is queen.

528
00:41:29,380 --> 00:41:30,700
They want another Stark prisoner,

529
00:41:30,700 --> 00:41:32,520
they can come and take me.

530
00:41:32,860 --> 00:41:35,390
Until then, I'll remain where I belong.

531
00:41:36,100 --> 00:41:37,730
I have work to do here.

532
00:41:40,350 --> 00:41:41,740
It's not safe.

533
00:41:42,110 --> 00:41:43,670
Ser Jaime will be there.

534
00:41:43,950 --> 00:41:46,030
You said he treated you honourably before.

535
00:41:46,380 --> 00:41:48,190
I'm not worried about me.

536
00:41:48,480 --> 00:41:51,320
It's not safe leaving you with Littlefinger.

537
00:41:51,760 --> 00:41:55,360
I have many guards who'd happily imprison him or behead him

538
00:41:55,360 --> 00:41:56,710
whether or not you're here.

539
00:41:56,710 --> 00:41:58,450
And you trust their loyalty?

540
00:41:59,120 --> 00:42:02,360
You trust he hasn't been speaking to them behind your back?

541
00:42:02,630 --> 00:42:06,200
Let me at least leave Podrick behind to watch over you.

542
00:42:06,200 --> 00:42:07,590
He has become a competent swordsman.

543
00:42:07,590 --> 00:42:11,880
I do not need to be watched over or minded or cared for.

544
00:42:12,230 --> 00:42:16,090
I'm not a child, I am the Lady of Winterfell and I am home.

545
00:42:16,260 --> 00:42:18,270
This is the safest place for me.

546
00:42:19,600 --> 00:42:20,610
My lady,

547
00:42:21,790 --> 00:42:24,910
I sworn an oath to protect you and your sister.

548
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:25,630
If I abandon you--

549
00:42:25,630 --> 00:42:27,820
The trip to King's Landing is long, Lady Brienne,

550
00:42:27,830 --> 00:42:30,110
and you won't be travelling on summer roads.

551
00:42:30,620 --> 00:42:31,450
The sooner you leave,

552
00:42:31,450 --> 00:42:33,640
the better your chances of making it on time.

553
00:42:36,940 --> 00:42:38,300
Yes, my lady.

554
00:43:01,080 --> 00:43:01,870
You can't.

555
00:43:03,530 --> 00:43:05,100
The most important person in the world

556
00:43:05,100 --> 00:43:07,650
can't fly off to the most dangerous place in the world.

557
00:43:07,780 --> 00:43:09,680
- Who else can? - No one.

558
00:43:09,890 --> 00:43:11,620
They knew the risk when they left.

559
00:43:11,950 --> 00:43:13,690
You can't win the throne if you're dead.

560
00:43:14,910 --> 00:43:16,680
You can't break the wheel if you're dead.

561
00:43:17,660 --> 00:43:20,340
- So what would you have me do? - Nothing.

562
00:43:21,080 --> 00:43:23,670
Sometimes nothing is the hardest thing to do.

563
00:43:25,480 --> 00:43:26,690
If you die

564
00:43:27,310 --> 00:43:28,920
we're all lost.

565
00:43:30,440 --> 00:43:32,090
Everyone, everything...

566
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:36,630
You told me to do nothing before and I've listened to you.

567
00:43:37,570 --> 00:43:39,110
I'm not doing nothing again.

568
00:44:36,330 --> 00:44:38,000
Dumb cunt.

569
00:44:59,400 --> 00:45:01,760
Fuck it.

570
00:47:35,630 --> 00:47:37,410
Fall back!

571
00:47:38,520 --> 00:47:40,050
Fall back!

572
00:47:40,050 --> 00:47:41,180
Come on!

573
00:48:07,560 --> 00:48:08,750
Help me!

574
00:51:21,660 --> 00:51:22,660
Jon!

575
00:53:13,340 --> 00:53:14,270
Go!

576
00:53:14,960 --> 00:53:17,330
Go now! Leave!

577
00:56:14,300 --> 00:56:15,450
Uncle Benjen!

578
00:56:16,310 --> 00:56:17,280
How?

579
00:56:19,910 --> 00:56:21,130
You ride for the pass.

580
00:56:21,340 --> 00:56:22,370
Come with me.

581
00:56:23,240 --> 00:56:24,220
There's no time.

582
00:56:24,730 --> 00:56:25,500
Go!

583
00:57:40,590 --> 00:57:42,000
We'll meet again, Clegane.

584
00:57:43,410 --> 00:57:44,680
Fucking hope not.

585
00:58:14,670 --> 00:58:16,610
It's time to go, Your Grace.

586
00:58:18,770 --> 00:58:19,860
A bit longer.

587
00:58:44,250 --> 00:58:45,870
Rider approaching!

588
00:58:54,690 --> 00:58:56,080
Open the gate!

589
01:00:39,100 --> 01:00:40,420
Not what you're looking for?

590
01:00:43,170 --> 01:00:45,870
I have hundreds of men here at Winterfell, all loyal to me.

591
01:00:48,200 --> 01:00:49,390
They're not here now.

592
01:00:52,180 --> 01:00:55,690
- What are these? - My faces.

593
01:00:58,630 --> 01:01:01,130
- Where did you get them? - In Braavos,

594
01:01:01,720 --> 01:01:03,860
while I was training to be a faceless man.

595
01:01:05,300 --> 01:01:06,370
What does that mean?

596
01:01:09,210 --> 01:01:12,850
Back in Braavos, before I got my first face,

597
01:01:13,920 --> 01:01:17,610
there was a game I used to play. The game of faces.

598
01:01:19,280 --> 01:01:22,340
It's simple-- I ask you a question about yourself

599
01:01:22,790 --> 01:01:25,030
and you try to make lies sound like the truth.

600
01:01:26,080 --> 01:01:28,300
If you fool me, you win.

601
01:01:29,340 --> 01:01:31,850
If I catch a lie, you lose.

602
01:01:32,960 --> 01:01:33,840
Let's play.

603
01:01:35,660 --> 01:01:36,920
I don't want to play.

604
01:01:38,320 --> 01:01:40,430
How do you feel about Jon being king?

605
01:01:42,270 --> 01:01:43,100
Is there someone else

606
01:01:43,100 --> 01:01:44,980
you think should rule the North instead of him?

607
01:01:44,980 --> 01:01:47,910
Those faces, what are they?

608
01:01:49,060 --> 01:01:50,350
You want to do the asking?

609
01:01:51,750 --> 01:01:52,790
Are you sure?

610
01:01:53,610 --> 01:01:55,210
The game of faces didn't turn out so well

611
01:01:55,210 --> 01:01:56,940
for the last person who asked me questions.

612
01:01:56,940 --> 01:01:58,570
Tell me what they are!

613
01:02:02,260 --> 01:02:04,780
We both wanted to be other people when we were younger.

614
01:02:06,520 --> 01:02:07,970
You wanted to be a queen.

615
01:02:08,960 --> 01:02:11,860
To sit next to a handsome young king on the Iron Throne.

616
01:02:13,350 --> 01:02:14,960
I wanted to be a knight

617
01:02:15,980 --> 01:02:18,630
to pick up a sword like father and go off to battle.

618
01:02:21,420 --> 01:02:23,710
Neither of us got to be that other person, did we?

619
01:02:25,310 --> 01:02:28,140
The world doesn't just let girls decide what they are going to be.

620
01:02:30,110 --> 01:02:33,820
But I can now. With the faces I can choose.

621
01:02:35,340 --> 01:02:36,920
I can become someone else.

622
01:02:38,570 --> 01:02:42,170
Speak in their voice, live in their skin.

623
01:02:45,630 --> 01:02:47,130
I could even become you.

624
01:02:55,310 --> 01:02:59,840
I wonder what it would feel like to wear those pretty dresses.

625
01:03:02,080 --> 01:03:03,810
To be the Lady of Winterfell.

626
01:03:06,910 --> 01:03:08,810
All I'd need to find out

627
01:03:11,270 --> 01:03:12,330
is your face.

628
01:04:11,350 --> 01:04:12,400
I'm sorry.

629
01:04:15,300 --> 01:04:16,870
I'm so sorry.

630
01:04:28,550 --> 01:04:30,370
I wish I could take it back.

631
01:04:32,910 --> 01:04:34,570
I wish we'd never go.

632
01:04:38,430 --> 01:04:39,320
I don't.

633
01:04:41,620 --> 01:04:43,500
If we hadn't gone I wouldn't have seen.

634
01:04:45,940 --> 01:04:47,390
You have to see it to know.

635
01:04:49,870 --> 01:04:50,890
Now I know.

636
01:04:54,710 --> 01:04:56,400
The dragons are my children.

637
01:04:57,680 --> 01:05:01,410
They're the only children I'll ever have. Do you understand?

638
01:05:08,080 --> 01:05:10,570
We are going to destroy the Night King and his army.

639
01:05:12,230 --> 01:05:13,500
And we'll do it together.

640
01:05:15,850 --> 01:05:17,160
You have my word.

641
01:05:21,110 --> 01:05:22,480
Thank you, Dany.

642
01:05:24,320 --> 01:05:25,090
Dany...

643
01:05:27,510 --> 01:05:29,390
Who was the last person who called me that?

644
01:05:31,480 --> 01:05:33,130
I'm not sure. Was it my brother?

645
01:05:35,350 --> 01:05:37,050
Not the company you want to keep.

646
01:05:38,620 --> 01:05:39,480
Alright.

647
01:05:41,510 --> 01:05:42,560
Not Dany.

648
01:05:47,090 --> 01:05:48,720
How about "My queen"?

649
01:05:52,500 --> 01:05:53,540
I'd...

650
01:05:54,410 --> 01:05:55,930
bend the knee but...

651
01:05:56,330 --> 01:05:58,450
What about those who swore allegiance to you?

652
01:05:58,760 --> 01:06:01,340
They'll all come to see you for what you are.

653
01:06:18,100 --> 01:06:19,660
I hope I deserve it.

654
01:06:21,720 --> 01:06:22,620
You do.

655
01:06:44,100 --> 01:06:45,560
You should get some rest.

